{"path": "guide-training-for-a-race.md", "content": "## Merlin

Merlin begins the journey with a focus on building a strong aerobic base. In the early weeks, runners should prioritize consistent, easy-paced runs to condition the heart and lungs while allowing the body to adapt to the increased load. Rest days are just as important as training days at this stage, giving muscles time to repair and strengthen. Cross-training activities like cycling or swimming can complement running without adding undue stress.
"}

{"path": "guide-making-cold-brew.md", "content": "## Linnet

Cold brew coffee is a smooth, low-acid alternative to traditional hot coffee, made by steeping coarse-ground beans in cold water for an extended period—typically 12 to 24 hours. The result is a concentrated, sweet-tasting brew that can be diluted with water or milk and served over ice. Unlike iced coffee, which is simply hot coffee cooled down, cold brew extracts flavors slowly without the bitterness that heat can bring out.
"}

{"path": "guide-training-for-a-race.md", "content": "## Merlin

Start your training with a solid foundation by building your aerobic base through consistent, easy-paced runs. Focus on gradually increasing your weekly mileage by no more than 10% to avoid injury, and include at least one long run each week to prepare your body for sustained effort.
"}

